    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0392" n="308" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg308"/>

                <head>No. 147.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Roustan to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the French Republic in the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1886-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 28, 1886</date>. (Received April
                    29.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The official journal of the Republic has
                    just published a notice informing the public with regard to the time allowed to
                    persons having claims on account of damages suffered during the recent conflict
                    between the French Government and the Hova Government, for the presentation of
                    the same, together with the documentary evidence in support thereof. I herewith
                    transmit to you the text of this notice, which I have just received from my
                    Government.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>TH. ROUSTAN.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d151-a1.xml" xpointer="d151-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
